.TH uxncli 1 "13 Aug 2026" "1.0" "Uxntal Reference Guide"
.SH NAME
uxncli \- Varvara virtual machine for the console
.SH SYNOPSIS
    uxncli \fIromfile\fP [ \fIargument\fP ]...
    uxncli \fB-v\fP
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uxncli is a console-only implementation of the Varvara virtual
machine. It is an emulator designed to run compatible ROM files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v Print version and exit
.SH VARVARA DEVICE SUPPORT
.SS System (\fB0x0\fP)
The system device is fully supported, although the color ports have no effect. The debugging port prints information on \fIstderr\fP.
.SS Console (\fB0x1\fP)
The console device is fully supported. Input from \fIstdin\fP is line-buffered, but output from \fIstdout\fP and \fIstderr\fP is unbuffered.
.SS Screen (\fB0x2\fP)
Unsupported.
.SS Audio (\fB0x3\fP through \fB0x6\fP)
Unsupported.
.SS Controller (\fB0x8\fP)
Unsupported.
.SS Mouse (\fB0x9\fP)
Unsupported.
.SS File (\fB0xa\fP and \fB0xb\fP)
The file device is fully supported. Paths are relative to the working directory and file access is not sandboxed.
.SS Datetime (\fB0xc\fP)
The date/time device is fully supported.
.SH NOTES
\fBuxncli\fP doesn't do any kind of text encoding. It is the job of
the ROM and caller to ensure that character encodings and terminal
control sequences match the underlying terminal (if any).
.PP
There is no way to disable the line-buffering of \fIstdin\fP, making
Uxncli inappropriate for interactive programs that need to respond to
individual keystrokes.
.PP
Uxncli doesn't implement a screen or audio device, so it lacks the
ability to do timer-based callbacks.
